      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "208f080dcbdeb37093650859f29d2b25c08057242a04e7600026ac90ab688533",
      "text": "On the way to Lake Atitlán, visit the archaeological site of Iximché near Tecpán.\\n\\nIximché was the capital of the Kaqchikel Maya. In 1524, the Spanish conquistador Pedro de Alvarado established Guatemala's first capital here.\\n\\nAfter exploring the site, continue to Lake Atitlán. Iximché is significant both as an archaeological monument and as a place connected with the early Spanish presence in Guatemala and Kaqchikel history.\\n\\n**Hotel:** Villa Santa Catarina.  \\n**Meals:** breakfast.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "model": "GPT-6",
        "runId": "ada-en-recover-20261110-maya",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The selected Word 2027 Day 3 covers Iximché and the transfer but omits the additional historical context in the approved RU narrative."
      }
    },
